# Agile Lifecycle Integration & Automated Test Case Generator

An automation utility engineered to programmatically transform acceptance criteria and raw application requirements into structured, validation-ready test configurations. By replacing manual asset creation with schema-mapped generation, this tool eliminates manual tracking overhead, enforces data consistency, and accelerates release readiness validation within enterprise pipelines.

## 🚀 The Problem & Solution

### The Challenge
In fast-paced enterprise environments, manual translation of product acceptance criteria into technical test suites introduces severe bottlenecks. Engineers spend critical hours manually scaffolding data structures, risking human error, inconsistent validation coverage, and poor alignment between initial product requirements and downstream system tests.

### The Solution
This programmatic engine ingests requirements payloads, parses logic models, and automatically outputs standardized test cases. It functions as a technical bridge within the software development lifecycle (SDLC)—ensuring strict schema mapping, deterministic structural generation, and immediate compatibility with enterprise tracking pipelines (such as Rally or automated execution engines).

## 🛠️ Core Capabilities & Technical Architecture

*   **Requirements to Schema Engine:** Parses arbitrary text or functional criteria, isolating functional logic blocks and transforming them into structured JSON test definitions.
*   **Deterministic Asset Scaffolding:** Generates comprehensive test coverage—including preconditions, explicit execution scripts, and strict verification checkpoints—using a unified, reliable factory design pattern.
*   **Enterprise Platform Alignment:** Outputs data formats ready for programmatic injection into REST APIs or direct migration into agile platform repositories, skipping UI layer latency.
*   **Defensive Design & Fault Tolerance:** Features a built-in validation layer that screens payloads for incomplete criteria, preventing downstream data corruption or malformed schema delivery.

## 💻 Tech Stack & Design Patterns

*   **Runtime Environment:** Node.js
*   **Core Engineering Language:** JavaScript (ES6+)
*   **Architecture Pattern:** Modular Factory Pattern & Separation of Concerns (Parsers decoupled from Schema Formatters)
*   **Test-Driven Development:** Automated suite validation powered by Jest (`npm test`)

